Adds an `Iterate` trait to capture the `.iter()` and `.iter_ref()` methods.

`Iterate[C, I, T]` is just a thin wrapper around `Cast[C, I], Iterator[I, T]`. Currently, it's not useful in a generic context; this will be addressed by #388.

`.iter()` is now automatically called by `for`, so instead of
```rs
for value in list.iter() {}
for &value in list.iter_ref() {}
```
one can now write
```rs
for value in list {}
for &value in &list {}
```

All PHP pages were failing with "Class EasyVol\App not found" due to incorrect instantiation. Navigation links used absolute paths breaking subdirectory installations.

## Changes

**App singleton pattern (43 files)**
- `new App()` → `App::getInstance()` (App constructor is private)
- Added missing `EasyVol\Autoloader::register()` calls
- Fixed method calls: `isAuthenticated()` → `isLoggedIn()`, `hasPermission()` → `checkPermission()`, `getDatabase()` → `getDb()`

**Path normalization**
- Navbar/sidebar: `/public/dashboard.php` → `dashboard.php`
- App redirects: `/public/login.php` → `login.php`

```php
// Before (fatal error)
require_once __DIR__ . '/../src/Autoloader.php';
use EasyVol\App;
$app = new App();
if (!$app->isAuthenticated()) {
    header('Location: /public/login.php');
}

// After
require_once __DIR__ . '/../src/Autoloader.php';
EasyVol\Autoloader::register();
use EasyVol\App;
$app = App::getInstance();
if (!$app->isLoggedIn()) {
    header('Location: login.php');
}
```

