Cardinal Warden game had multiplicative HP scaling causing difficulty spikes, lost input handlers on tab switches, reset dark mode on restart, and lacked restart confirmation.

## Changes

### Wave HP Scaling
Changed from multiplicative (`wave + 1`) to additive (`1 + wave * 0.1`):
```javascript
// Before: Wave 2 = 2x HP, Wave 20 = 20x HP
const waveMultiplier = this.wave + 1;

// After: Wave 2 = 1.1x HP, Wave 20 = 2x HP  
const waveMultiplier = 1 + (this.wave * 0.1);
```

### Tab Visibility Input Fix
Added visibility change handler to re-attach pointer event listeners when tab regains focus:
```javascript
handleVisibilityChange() {
  if (document.visibilityState === 'visible') {
    this.detachInputHandlers();
    this.attachInputHandlers();
  }
}
```

### Dark Mode Persistence
Pass `nightMode` from visual settings to simulation constructor:
```javascript
const visualSettings = getShinVisualSettings();
cardinalSimulation = new CardinalWardenSimulation({
  nightMode: visualSettings.nightMode,
  // ...
});
```

### Restart Confirmation
Two-click pattern with 3-second timeout:
- First click: Shows "Progress will be lost, confirm?" in red
- Second click: Confirms restart
- Timeout: Auto-resets to original state

