Addresses performance, safety, and maintainability issues identified in the PR #8 review comments.

## Performance Optimizations
- Pass string and vector parameters by const reference throughout DAL layer (eliminates unnecessary copies in hot paths like `loadTickets`, `saveSeats`, `Split`, `Join`)
- Remove redundant object construction in `TicketDAL::saveTickets` (direct `push_back` instead of copying all 8 fields)

## Type Safety
- Replace `int` loop variables with `size_t` to fix signed/unsigned comparison warnings
- Add underflow protection in `CurrencyFormat::formatCurrency` loop

## Error Handling
- Wrap `std::stoi` in try-catch for `std::invalid_argument` and `std::out_of_range`
- Include exception details in error messages

## Code Clarity
- Rename loop variables: `tickets` → `ticketItem`, `updateSeat` → `seat` (singular form for iteration)
- Fix `.vscode/launch.json` to use `${workspaceFolder}` instead of hardcoded absolute paths

### Example Changes

**Before:**
```cpp
bool TicketDAL::saveTickets(string fileName, Ticket ticket) {
    vector<Ticket> ticketBooked = loadTickets(fileName);
    Ticket newTicket;
    newTicket._ticketID = ticket._ticketID;
    // ... copy all 8 fields
    ticketBooked.push_back(newTicket);
    for(Ticket tickets : ticketBooked) { /* ... */ }
}
```

**After:**
```cpp
bool TicketDAL::saveTickets(const string& fileName, const Ticket& ticket) {
    vector<Ticket> ticketBooked = loadTickets(fileName);
    ticketBooked.push_back(ticket);
    for(const Ticket& ticketItem : ticketBooked) { /* ... */ }
}
```

